            <div xml:id="d906">

                <pb facs="0820" n="813" xml:id="pg813"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11664: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-16T18:00:00+09:00">December 16, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 16—10:23 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>644. Our 595, December 4, 8 p.m. A conference between the Government and Imperial
                    Headquarters which began on the 14th and was continued yesterday and today is
                    reported to be discussing matters of high national policy. It is generally
                    understood that if a consensus of opinion can be reached the Cabinet will
                    tomorrow consider requesting that the Emperor call a conference in the near
                    future.</p>
                <p>In view of the trend of discussion in the press which is speculative and of
                    certain information brought to me, I am inclined to think that a declaration of
                    war is not imminent.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
